{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "root": {
    "type": "Grid",
    "props": {
      "columns": 12,
      "gap": 16
    },
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "summary_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "variant": "hero"
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "summary"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "KPIStrip",
            "id": "summary_kpi",
            "props": {
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Duplicate occurrences",
                  "field": "finding_count",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Affected files",
                  "field": "affected_files",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Healed",
                  "field": "healed_count",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Kept original",
                  "field": "kept_count",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Still absorbed",
                  "field": "absorbed_remaining",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Merge absorptions",
                  "field": "merge_absorbed",
                  "format": "count"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "findings_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "Colliding objects (UUID-precise)",
          "keepChildrenOnEmpty": true
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "findings"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Table",
            "id": "findings_table",
            "props": {
              "rowKey": "row_key",
              "density": "comfortable",
              "sortable": true,
              "searchable": "auto",
              "pageParam": "page",
              "searchParam": "q",
              "sortParam": "sort",
              "clientMode": true,
              "searchAutoThreshold": 3,
              "searchPlaceholder": "Search file, container, text or UUID…",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "field": "file",
                  "label": "File"
                },
                {
                  "field": "type",
                  "label": "Type",
                  "format": "badge"
                },
                {
                  "field": "parent",
                  "label": "Container"
                },
                {
                  "field": "position",
                  "label": "Position"
                },
                {
                  "field": "display",
                  "label": "Object (decoded)"
                },
                {
                  "field": "occ",
                  "label": "Occ.",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "heal_status",
                  "label": "Heal status",
                  "format": "badge"
                },
                {
                  "field": "dup_uuid",
                  "label": "UUID",
                  "align": "center",
                  "format": "copy"
                }
              ],
              "onRowClick": {
                "action": "openObject",
                "args": {
                  "uuid": "{{nav_uuid}}",
                  "type": "{{nav_type}}",
                  "file": "{{file}}",
                  "step": "{{step_uuid}}"
                }
              },
              "empty": {
                "message": "No UUID-precise duplicate details captured — the import census found no intra-file duplicates."
              },
              "alwaysShowCount": true
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "merge_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "Merge absorptions (chunk overlap or clone file with identical internal name)"
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "merge_absorptions"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Table",
            "id": "merge_table",
            "props": {
              "rowKey": "row_key",
              "density": "compact",
              "sortable": true,
              "searchable": "auto",
              "searchAutoThreshold": 3,
              "searchPlaceholder": "Search table or file…",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "field": "table_name",
                  "label": "Catalog table"
                },
                {
                  "field": "file",
                  "label": "File"
                },
                {
                  "field": "absorbed",
                  "label": "Absorbed",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "run_at",
                  "label": "Merge run",
                  "format": "date:relative"
                }
              ],
              "empty": {
                "message": "No duplicates were absorbed at merge time."
              },
              "alwaysShowCount": true
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "stats_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "Census cross-check per catalog and file"
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "absorption_stats"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Table",
            "id": "stats_table",
            "props": {
              "rowKey": "row_key",
              "density": "compact",
              "sortable": true,
              "searchable": "auto",
              "searchAutoThreshold": 3,
              "searchPlaceholder": "Search catalog or file…",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "field": "catalog",
                  "label": "Catalog"
                },
                {
                  "field": "file",
                  "label": "File"
                },
                {
                  "field": "source_records",
                  "label": "Source records",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "stored_rows",
                  "label": "Stored rows",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "absorbed",
                  "label": "Absorbed",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "coverage",
                  "label": "Detail coverage",
                  "format": "badge"
                }
              ],
              "empty": {
                "message": "The import census reports no absorbed duplicates."
              },
              "alwaysShowCount": true
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "notes_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "About this check"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Markdown",
            "id": "notes_md",
            "props": {
              "content": "A UUID assigned to **two objects inside one file** is a source defect of the FileMaker export (typically copy/paste with old FileMaker versions against newer files). FM-Lab's import keeps exactly one object per UUID (deterministic, last write wins) — the absorbed objects therefore **no longer exist in the catalog**. The columns *Container*, *Position* and *Object (decoded)* are their only remaining trace; use them to locate both objects in FileMaker. Clicking a row opens the surviving object.\n\n**Merge absorptions** are a separate class: duplicates absorbed when the converter merges file chunks. Their root cause is not distinguishable after the fact — either converter-internal chunk overlap (no solution defect) or clone files sharing the same internal file name (a genuine collision).\n\n**There is no automatic fix.** Claris' repair mode assigns entirely new UUIDs and breaks every external UUID reference; the correction must happen in the source file. Duplicates of the same UUID *across* files are covered by the companion dashboard **UUID Clone Collisions**. Data source is the import census — the numbers reflect the state of the last XML import."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
